an (≤55 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332046"} "Lightweight, Greco-Roman (≤60 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332092"} "Welterweight, Greco-Roman (≤66 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332138"} "Middleweight, Greco-Roman (≤74 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332184"} "Light-Heavyweight, Greco-Roman (≤84 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332230"} "Heavyweight, Greco-Roman (≤96 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332276"} "Super-Heavyweight, Greco-Roman (≤120 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332322"} "Featherweight, Freestyle (≤55 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332368"} "Lightweight, Freestyle (≤60 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332414"} "Welterweight, Freestyle (≤66 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332460"} "Middleweight, Freestyle (≤74 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332506"} "Light-Heavyweight, Freestyle (≤84 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332552"} "Heavyweight, Freestyle (≤96 kg), Men"] "\n" [:option {:value "332644"} "Flyweight, Freestyle (≤48 kg), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "332690"} "Lightweight, Freestyle (≤55 kg), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "332736"} "Middleweight, Freestyle (≤63 kg), Women"] "\n" [:option {:value "332782"} "Heavyweight, Freestyle (≤72 kg), Women"]] [:script {} "$('#same_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#same_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:form {:class "form-inline form-inline-header"} [:select {:name "id", :id "other_games_select", :class "form-control"} [:option {:value ""} "In other Games"] "\n" [:option {:value "126798"} "1972"] "\n" [:option {:value "127646"} "1976"] "\n" [:option {:value "128414"} "1980"] "\n" [:option {:value "129169"} "1984"] "\n" [:option {:value "130229"} "1988"] "\n" [:option {:value "131322"} "1992"] "\n" [:option {:value "132402"} "1996"] "\n" [:option {:value "133294"} "2000"] "\n" [:option {:value "133925"} "2004"] "\n" [:option {:value "263407"} "2008"] "\n" [:option {:value "355450"} "2016"] "\n" [:option {:value "19009619"} "2020"] "\n" [:option {:value "2008093"} "2024"]] [:script {} "$('#other_games_select').change(function(){location.href='/results/' + $('#other_games_select').val();})"]] " | " [:a {:href "/event_names/677"} "Event type"]] [:h1 {:class "event_title"} "Super-Heavyweight, Freestyle (≤120 kg), Men" [:small {}]] [:table {:class "biodata"} [:tbody {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Date"] [:td {} "11 August 2012"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Status"] [:td {} "Olympic"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Location"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/venues/861"} "ExCeL, Newham, London"] " (North Arena 2)"]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Participants"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/events/332597"} "18 from 18 countries"]]] [:tr {} [:th {} "Format"] [:td {:colspan "2"} "Single elimination tournament. Competitors losing to the finalists entered repechage tournament for bronze medals."]]]] [:div {:class "description"} [:p {} "Since his first appearance at the Olympic Games in 2000, " [:a {:href "/athletes/95185"} "Artur Taymazov"] " of Uzbekistan had reached the finals of the men’s super-heavyweight freestyle wrestling tournament every time and had lost only once, in his first attempt. He was also a two time World Champion (2003 and 2006) and runner-up (2001 and 2010), twice Asian Champion (2000 and 2011), and three-time Asian Games gold medalist (2002, 2006, and 2010). Nonetheless he was expected to have some significant challengers at the 2012 Summer Olympics, most notably " [:a {:href "/athletes/120368"} "Bilyal Makhov"] " of Russia, a three-time (2007, 2009, 2010) World Champion and 2010 European Champion. Makhov lost his world title in 2011 to " [:a {:href "/athletes/121580"} "Aleksey Shemarov"] " of Belarus, however, who would also be looking to challenge Taymazov in the final. Not to be counted out was " [:a {:href "/athletes/124609"} "Taha Akgül"] " of Turkey, the reigning European Champion."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Taymazov was drawn into a relatively easy half that included Shemarov, who was defeated by " [:a {:href "/athletes/126748"} "Tervel Dlagnev"] " of the United States, the 2011 Pan American Champion. Taymazov pinned Dlagnev in the semi-finals and went on to meet " [:a {:href "/athletes/122324"} "Davit Modzmanashvili"] " of Georgia in the gold medal match. Modzmanashvili was a bronze medalist at the most recent World and European Championships who had returned from a doping violation in 2008 and defeated " [:a {:href "/athletes/120368"} "Bilyal Makhov"] " in the semi-finals of the London tournament. In the final, Taymazov proved himself once again to be worthy of Olympic Gold, winning the first round " [:em {} "par terre"] " by successfully reversing Modzmanashvili’s advantage and pushing the Georgian out of the ring in the second period for an unanswered point that earned him the Olympic crown."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The first bronze medal match pitted Dlagnev against " [:a {:href "/athletes/122826"} "Komeil Ghasemi"] " of Iran, runner up to Taymazov at the most recent Asian Championships. Ghasemi wasted no time in the first period, winning it within the first 20 seconds by scoring four points that would remain unanswered. The second period went to " [:em {} "par terre"] ", where the American drew the advantage and converted it into a point, but the Iranian was able to push his opponent out of the ring in the final ten seconds of the last round to earn the bronze. The final podium spot was decided between Makhov and " [:a {:href "/athletes/126718"} "Daulet Shabanbay"] " of Kazakhstan, who had won his first his first major international medal at the age of 14 in the heavyweight division of the 2008 Asian Championships and repeated the feat in 2009 and 2011 before moving up to the super-heavyweight class. Makhov’s experience was on display in the first period, scoring five unanswered points, but Shabanbay responded in the second round with a three-point shutout of his own. In the final period, the three-time World Champion was simply the better wrestler, and won the medal with a 3-0 score."] "\n\n" [:p {} "That was how the event and the results seemed to have ended. In 2015, however, the IOC began re-testing samples from the 2008 Beijing and 2012 London Olympics, using newer, more advanced testing techniques, in an effort to find those who had used performance enhancing drugs (PEDs), but in whom it could not be detected at the time of those Olympics. This was one of the many events affected."] "\n\n" [:p {} "The original silver medalist, Davit Modzanashvili of Georgia, was later disqualified when he was revealed to have a re-test positive for both dehydrochloromethyltestosterone (turinabol) and stanozolol. His silver medal was removed. In July 2019, the gold medalist, Artur Taymazov of Uzbekistan was similarly disqualified when a re-test of his doping sample showed evidence of dehydrochloromethyltestosterone (turinabol) metabolites. In February 2020, the IOC ruled on the final standings and medals and awarded gold medals to both Ghasemi and Makhov, while Dlagnev and Shabanbay became the bronze medalists. Dlagnev received his bronze medal on 6 March 2022 at the 2022 Big 10 Conference Wrestling Championships."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitor"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/122826"} "Komeil Ghasemi"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/IRI"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/IRI.png"}] "IRI"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/120368"} "Bilyal Makhov"]] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/RUS"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/RUS.png"}] "RUS"]] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "=3"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/athletes/126748"}